e stalk is $452$ centimeters tall, and Alice observed that its height increases by $5\\%$ every day.  How tall was the plant $2$ weeks ago when she first noticed it growing? Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9ee1045d7be84623184b590889c00ffb0b0104bf7e340bef1ff367d532ff68cc"},"seconds":22.603009939193726,"seed":1124707533943631081,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to work backwards from today's height of the bean plant, considering the daily growth rate.\n\nGiven:\n- Current height of the plant = \\( 452 \\) centimeters\n- Daily growth rate = \\( 5\\% \\) per day\n- Time elapsed since Alice first noticed the plant = \\( 2 \\) weeks \\( = 14 \\) days\n\nLet \\( h \\) be the height of the plant when Alice first noticed it 14 days ago.\n\nSince the height increases by \\( 5\\% \\) each day, the height at the end of each day can be expressed as:\n\\[ h_{\\text{new}} = h_{\\text{old}} \\times 1.05 \\]\n\nAfter 14 days, the height of the plant is:\n\\[ 452 = h \\times (1.05)^{14} \\]\n\nTo find \\( h \\), we need to isolate it by dividing both sides by \\( (1.05)^{14} \\):\n\\[ h = \\frac{452}{(1.05)^{14}} \\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\( (1.05)^{14} \\):\n\\[ (1.05)^{14} \\approx 1.979932 \\]\n\nNow, divide 452 by this value:\n\\[ h = \\frac{452}{1.979932} \\approx 228.4 \\]\n\nThus, the height of the plant when Alice first noticed it was approximately \\( 228.4 \\) centimeters.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{228.4} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{228.4}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
